================================================================================
Model weights
================================================================================

This product does not redistribute model weights. No `.onnx`, `.safetensors`
or `.bin` file is in this repository, and `ci/budget.py` counts only the
`pamin` binary and the native libraries it links, so a release artifact
contains no model. Weights are fetched from the Hugging Face hub the first
time a command asks for one, into a cache under the workspace, by the user's
own machine.

That distinction is what the list below is scoped by. These licences govern
what a user downloads and runs when they search.
They are not distribution terms for anything this project ships, and adding a
model does not move the size budget.

One of the exports carries no licence tag of its own. That is recorded here
rather than smoothed over: a re-export with no tag is usable when the chain to
a licensed source is readable, and the chain is given for it.

Embedding models
----------------

  gpahal/bge-m3-onnx-int8                              MIT
    The embedding model. An int8 export of BAAI/bge-m3, itself MIT.

Reranker models
---------------

  pamin-labs/bge-reranker-v2-m3-sq-int8-onnx           Apache-2.0
    The reranker, pinned to cfa01c1989db3c5cc3a720a495e86966de9b4d6b.
    Modified by PaminLabs from onnx-community/bge-reranker-v2-m3-ONNX at
    6f5ff65298512715a1e669753bc754d2bc8f367b: the int8 weights re-quantized
    from the fp32 export with SmoothQuant (alpha 0.75) on the q/k/v and first
    feed-forward inputs. That is an ONNX re-export of BAAI/bge-reranker-v2-m3,
    itself Apache-2.0.

================================================================================
Rust dependencies
================================================================================

`deny.toml` holds the licence policy for the crate graph and
`cargo deny check licenses` enforces it in CI. That is a separate question
from the models above and the file says so: a crate is linked into the binary
this project distributes, where a model is not.

One entry there is worth naming here too. `option-ext`, reached through
`dirs`, is MPL-2.0 — weak copyleft at file granularity. It is linked
unmodified from crates.io, so its own source stays available under its own
terms and nothing about this project's Apache-2.0 licence is affected. The
allowance is deliberate and is explained where it is granted.
